WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.770
Priorities become real when they receive time, attention, and review.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:09.641
A goal written in a document but never reflected on the calendar is mostly a wish.

00:00:09.641 --> 00:00:13.678
That does not mean every priority must become a rigid block.

00:00:13.678 --> 00:00:18.815
It means the system should show whether important work has a path to happen.

00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:22.118
If the calendar only contains meetings and urgent requests,

00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:24.687
it may not represent the actual priorities.

00:00:24.687 --> 00:00:29.457
Outcome goals describe the result: ship the project, improve a skill, reduce incidents,

00:00:29.457 --> 00:00:32.026
strengthen a relationship, or complete a certification.

00:00:32.026 --> 00:00:36.429
Process commitments describe the recurring behavior that makes the result more likely:

00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:41.200
two focused build sessions each week, a weekly review, thirty minutes of study,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.136
or a maintenance window that actually stays protected.

00:00:44.136 --> 00:00:45.237
Outcomes give direction.

00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:46.704
Process commitments create traction.

00:00:46.704 --> 00:00:50.741
Time horizons help balance the near term and the long term.

00:00:50.741 --> 00:00:53.310
Daily planning helps choose the next actions.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.511
Weekly planning exposes collisions and capacity.

00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:59.181
Monthly planning identifies larger commitments, travel, deadlines, and review points.

00:00:59.181 --> 00:01:04.319
Long-term planning asks whether current time use is compounding toward a future that matters.

00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:08.722
Without multiple horizons, the urgent present tends to consume the strategic future.

00:01:08.722 --> 00:01:10.924
High-leverage activities produce progress that compounds.

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:14.961
They might include designing a reusable process, learning a core skill,

00:01:14.961 --> 00:01:17.896
fixing a recurring failure, improving documentation, mentoring someone,

00:01:17.896 --> 00:01:22.667
exercising judgment before work begins, or protecting a focused block for difficult creation.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:25.603
Productive motion can feel satisfying without changing outcomes.

00:01:25.603 --> 00:01:30.740
Meaningful progress moves the work, the capability, or the relationship in a durable direction.
